From b839c0a2b5102ca2846bfa0dd08bc84c14fd4675 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Anthony <markususeche@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:35:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] audio: pace render callbacks to real time (fixes Dante 1100
 audio); per-frame audio diagnostics behind audio_diagnostics

The audio worker ran 2-4 guest render callbacks back to back whenever the device
pulled several frames at once. Dante's Inferno's mixer only had new data for every
other 512-sample block in such a burst (2 frames sound, 2 silent = 1100), on iPhone
and on macOS arm64 and x86_64 alike. Callbacks now run one per 5.33 ms, keeping
about 8 frames queued at the device (audio_pace_callbacks, default on).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
